  [type] E0180

  × `return` is not allowed in the initializer of global `EARLY_EXIT` — an initializer is an expression, not a function body; its value is its last expression (move early exits into a helper
  │ function)
    ╭─[initializers.baml:42:9]
 42 │         return 1;
    ·         ─────────
    ╰────

  [type] E0182

  × global `SPAWNED` uses `spawn` — top-level declarations are evaluated once at startup (`$init`), before anything can be scheduled or waited on; compute the value synchronously, or move the
  │ concurrent work into the function that needs it
    ╭─[initializers.baml:56:17]
 56 │ const SPAWNED = spawn { 1 };
    ·                 ───────────
    ╰────

  [type] E0182

  × global `AWAITED` reaches `await` through `waits` — top-level declarations are evaluated once at startup (`$init`), before anything can be scheduled or waited on; compute the value synchronously,
  │ or move the concurrent work into the function that needs it
    ╭─[initializers.baml:64:17]
 64 │ const AWAITED = waits();
    ·                 ─────
    ╰────

  [type] E0163

  × global `HOME` calls `baml.env.get`, which performs io — top-level declarations are evaluated at startup (`$init`), where io is unavailable; resolve at request time instead — e.g. `env.X`, a
  │ late-bound reference read only when the request is made
    ╭─[initializers.baml:67:14]
 67 │ const HOME = baml.env.get("HOME");
    ·              ────────────
    ╰────

  [type] E0183

  ⚠ global `UNCAUGHT` can throw `string` while it is initialized — globals are evaluated once, at startup, and an uncaught throw there stops the program from starting; if that is not intended,
  │ handle it in the initializer with `catch`
    ╭─[initializers.baml:74:7]
 74 │ const UNCAUGHT = may_fail();
    ·       ────────
    ╰────
